!.vscode/extensions.json

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Dead-code audit scratch (knip/jscpd outputs, type-check dumps, tier scripts) —
# transient, regenerated on demand. knip.json (the config) IS committed.
_audit-*
_typecheck.txt
_t2*
_tier*
# Transient cut checklist — lives in the Obsidian vault, not shipped to main.
CUT-LIST.md
_design-reference/

# Understand-anything knowledge graph (derived artifact, rebuilt nightly)
.understand-anything/
.superpowers/

# Security audit reports — findings name unfixed weaknesses and live table/
# function names. This repo goes public at Phase 4, so they stay local.
.gstack/

# Internal working documents — kept on disk, not published.
#
# Implementation plans, design specs, session handoffs and integration designs
# are process artefacts: they capture how we got somewhere, name commercial
# partners, and go stale the moment the code moves on. The repo flips public at
# Phase 4, so the only markdown that ships is README.md and the agent-discovery
# files the site serves from public/. Everything else (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md,
# CONTEXT.md, ADRs, specs) is local to the maintainer's checkout and never
# ships in a clone. A new public doc (SECURITY.md, CHANGELOG.md) needs its own
# !/NAME.md line below.
#
# NOTE: untracking these does NOT remove them from git history. Anything
# already committed is still reachable via `git log`. If a specific document
# must not be in the public history, it needs `git filter-repo` before the
# Phase 4 flip.
*.md
!/README.md
!/public/**/*.md
docs/handoffs/
docs/plans/
docs/runbooks/
docs/onesearch/
docs/superpowers/
MOVE_NARRATOR_FRONTEND_HANDOFF.md

# Design handoff mockups (reference HTML + assets, not shipped app code)
design_handoff_*/

# Throwaway UI prototypes. This repo goes public at Phase 4, so exploratory
# routes and placeholder imagery must never reach history. Rebuild anything
# worth keeping as a real page instead of restoring a /prototype/* route.
src/pages/prototype/
public/prototype/

# Supabase CLI scratch dir (holds the linked project ref + version cache)
supabase/.temp/

# Backups of env files — never let one land in the repo
.env*.bak*
.env*.backup*

# Archives. This repo goes public at Phase 4 and design/handoff bundles are
# dropped in the root by hand, so a bare `git add .` must never sweep one in.
*.zip

# graft's local graph cache — regenerable, not committed (run `graft build`).
/graft/

# Web Bot Auth private signing key (scripts/web-bot-auth-keygen.mjs)
**/private*.jwk.json

# Local tooling state. dfx build output is regenerated on every deploy, and
# settings.local.json holds one developer's machine-specific permissions.
.dfx/
.claude/settings.local.json
